WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.305 --> 00:00:04.576
(upbeat ukulele music)

00:00:04.576 --> 00:00:08.070
(Skype calling sound)

00:00:12.409 --> 00:00:14.444
- Yeah, hello!

00:00:14.444 --> 00:00:16.094
- There's a giant hand on the screen.

00:00:16.094 --> 00:00:21.094
- Oh hey, Mom, can you
make yourself landscape?

00:00:21.347 --> 00:00:22.175
There we go!

00:00:22.175 --> 00:00:23.776
- You're on camera now.

00:00:23.776 --> 00:00:26.888
- OK, you are filming now, right?

00:00:26.888 --> 00:00:28.887
- [Eugene] Yes, you look very beautiful.

00:00:28.887 --> 00:00:31.322
- Oh, thank you. I don't think so.

00:00:31.322 --> 00:00:33.355
- So how are you? We never
really FaceTime, you and I.

00:00:33.355 --> 00:00:34.956
- [Zach] We talk on the
phone a bunch, but we never,

00:00:34.956 --> 00:00:37.324
I never think to FaceTime you,
it's nice to like, see you.

00:00:37.324 --> 00:00:39.834
- [Keith] So we're all
Skyping with our mothers

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:41.157
to talk about motherhood.

00:00:41.157 --> 00:00:42.373
- [Zach] We've been
shooting this big series

00:00:42.373 --> 00:00:44.179
of videos exploring parenthood.

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:45.124
- How are you finding it?

00:00:45.124 --> 00:00:47.484
- [Ned] How am I finding it? (laughs)

00:00:47.484 --> 00:00:48.804
- Well, I, uhm...

00:00:48.804 --> 00:00:50.894
- I learned a lot about what you had

00:00:50.894 --> 00:00:52.567
to go through three times.

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:54.981
- Like, I knew that being
a parent was really hard,

00:00:54.981 --> 00:00:56.699
but it's so fucking hard.

00:00:56.699 --> 00:00:58.672
- Some of the things that we've done:

00:00:58.672 --> 00:01:02.714
we started with wearing
fake pregnancy bellies.

00:01:02.714 --> 00:01:06.010
- [Eugene] There's something
called "labor pain simulation."

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.380
- Then we got to play with a baby,

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.563
which was the cutest baby in the world.

00:01:09.563 --> 00:01:12.303
- So we also, you know,
remember when we had

00:01:12.303 --> 00:01:13.951
those robot babies in school?

00:01:13.951 --> 00:01:15.990
- [Keith's mom] (laughs) Yes!

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:17.800
- [Keith] We had to have
those robot babies again.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.124
(Keith's mom laughs)

00:01:19.124 --> 00:01:20.818
- So I was wondering what, you know,

00:01:20.818 --> 00:01:25.818
what your pregnancy was like,
what having me was like.

00:01:26.182 --> 00:01:28.343
- Pregnancy with you was tough.

00:01:28.343 --> 00:01:29.805
- No, it wasn't difficult.

00:01:29.805 --> 00:01:32.846
- You know, you didn't kick me.

00:01:32.846 --> 00:01:34.193
- You used to run in place.

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.052
- Oh, OK!

00:01:35.052 --> 00:01:38.357
- I gave birth in the
summer, and I was, you

00:01:38.357 --> 00:01:40.098
get very hot at the end.
- [Zach] Ugh!

00:01:40.098 --> 00:01:43.117
And I also got very fat.

00:01:43.117 --> 00:01:45.461
- So I made you fat and sweaty?

00:01:45.461 --> 00:01:47.388
- You did indeed.

00:01:47.388 --> 00:01:50.686
- The doctor told me
your heartbeat is faster,

00:01:50.686 --> 00:01:55.445
so everybody, including
doctor, thought you were girl.

00:01:55.445 --> 00:02:00.089
- Oh! (laughs) You thought
I was a very silent girl?

00:02:00.089 --> 00:02:02.040
- Yes, yes.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.578
- At one point, I had to,
I had to have bedrest,

00:02:06.578 --> 00:02:08.680
so you and I watched a
lot of old "I Love Lucy"s.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:09.725
- Oh!

00:02:09.725 --> 00:02:11.935
- You liked like feeling when I kicked?

00:02:11.935 --> 00:02:12.861
- Totally.

00:02:12.861 --> 00:02:15.172
- It wasn't like, "What is
this monster inside of me?"

00:02:15.172 --> 00:02:16.390
- I loved it 'cause it made it real.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:18.411
- Right. Yeah, we didn't
have a real thing,

00:02:18.411 --> 00:02:22.010
we just had a little pouch with baby goo.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.332
- What was it like when you delivered me?

00:02:24.332 --> 00:02:26.143
- I mean, was that the most painful thing

00:02:26.143 --> 00:02:27.072
you've ever experienced?

00:02:27.072 --> 00:02:28.744
- It was awful, I was screaming.

00:02:28.744 --> 00:02:30.881
I think the whole hospital
must have heard me.

00:02:30.881 --> 00:02:35.040
- Well, down the hall, there
were these women screaming!

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.497
- (laughs nervously) Oh no!

00:02:36.497 --> 00:02:40.793
- Some pain, but you know,
you know, I love kids.

00:02:40.793 --> 00:02:43.997
- And at one point,
your heart rate dropped.

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:48.153
And, it wasn't scary, but I guess,

00:02:48.153 --> 00:02:50.823
something was going on
that they said to me,

00:02:50.823 --> 00:02:52.867
"OK", and you know, it
was far enough along,

00:02:52.867 --> 00:02:55.073
they said, "Alright, we
gotta get him out now."

00:02:55.073 --> 00:02:59.038
- In your case, I had
you in fifteen minutes.

00:02:59.038 --> 00:03:01.222
(Keith laughs wildly)

00:03:01.222 --> 00:03:03.706
I went from 5 to 10 in fifteen minutes

00:03:03.706 --> 00:03:05.702
in little bitty ol' Smith County Hospital.

00:03:05.702 --> 00:03:07.327
- [Eugene] You know, I'd
never held a baby before.

00:03:07.327 --> 00:03:09.055
- Oh, you never?

00:03:09.055 --> 00:03:09.627
- No!

00:03:09.627 --> 00:03:12.709
- I had my first experience
changing a diaper.

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:14.613
- You remember the first
diaper you ever changed?

00:03:14.613 --> 00:03:16.957
- Oh, yeah! It was - I
didn't tell them about it.

00:03:16.957 --> 00:03:18.188
- You made mittens!

00:03:18.188 --> 00:03:19.907
- Yeah, I made like, paper towel mittens

00:03:19.907 --> 00:03:21.276
so I wouldn't get poop on my hands,

00:03:21.276 --> 00:03:23.274
'cause I was like twelve.

00:03:23.274 --> 00:03:25.665
- Did I poop a lot?

00:03:25.665 --> 00:03:27.360
- Every baby poops a lot.

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.101
- How was I like when I was a little baby?

00:03:29.101 --> 00:03:31.550
Was I crying a lot?

00:03:31.550 --> 00:03:33.463
- Oh no, you didn't cry.

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:37.062
- You liked music, so we
played this tape dad had

00:03:37.062 --> 00:03:38.054
called "Trumpet a Go-Go."

00:03:38.054 --> 00:03:39.215
- You were a good baby, you always

00:03:39.215 --> 00:03:43.165
made everybody smile and
laugh! You were just like now.

00:03:43.165 --> 00:03:44.500
- Sounds like me.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.233
- Well 'ama', it's Mother's Day.

00:03:48.233 --> 00:03:49.256
- Oh, yes!

00:03:49.256 --> 00:03:51.879
- So, I wanted to call you
and say that I love you.

00:03:51.879 --> 00:03:54.945
- You know, I tell you I love you a lot,

00:03:54.945 --> 00:03:57.383
I hope I do. I hope you know
it, I think you know it.

00:03:57.383 --> 00:04:00.029
- All of these things
that we've done have been,

00:04:00.029 --> 00:04:03.234
like, simulations, right? They
haven't been the real thing.

00:04:03.234 --> 00:04:06.424
- Is there anything else
that you experienced

00:04:06.424 --> 00:04:09.937
during motherhood that was significant?

00:04:09.937 --> 00:04:11.186
- Like what?

00:04:11.186 --> 00:04:14.066
- (laughs) I don't know,
I'm not a mom! I don't know.

00:04:14.066 --> 00:04:16.569
- We did this whole thing
to just try and like see

00:04:16.569 --> 00:04:19.031
if we could understand what
it's like to be a parent,

00:04:19.031 --> 00:04:20.539
what it's like to be a mother,

00:04:20.539 --> 00:04:24.340
and what I realize is,
I mean, I'll never know.

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.198
- Through this process, I've been able

00:04:26.198 --> 00:04:28.381
to imagine the bigger
picture a little bit.

00:04:28.381 --> 00:04:33.381
- Don't let the Try Guys'
Mother's Day videos scare you.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:37.110
Whatever you go through,
it's well worth it,

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:41.010
and it's awesome to be a
mother and look at these kids!

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:43.611
Look what I raised. I'm so lucky.

00:04:43.611 --> 00:04:47.627
- Raising kids is a real joy. It's joyful

00:04:47.627 --> 00:04:52.627
and it's [inaudible]. I believe that.

00:04:52.787 --> 00:04:56.169
- Parenting is full-time,
24 hours, all the time.

00:04:56.169 --> 00:04:58.769
- And I'm always, always
happy to be your mother.

00:04:58.769 --> 00:04:59.884
- Thank you.

00:04:59.884 --> 00:05:02.907
(soft sobs)

00:05:07.737 --> 00:05:09.147
- Are you really crying?!

00:05:09.147 --> 00:05:14.147
- Yeah, I don't know. I love you so much.

00:05:14.395 --> 00:05:16.136
- I love you too, sweetie.

00:05:16.136 --> 00:05:19.085
- You're like the best
person in the entire world,

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:20.478
you're so important to me.

00:05:20.478 --> 00:05:22.819
- Thanks for giving birth to me.

00:05:22.819 --> 00:05:24.139
- OK, thank you, you're welcome.

00:05:24.139 --> 00:05:26.555
- Happy Mother's Day on
Sunday! I'll call you though.

00:05:26.555 --> 00:05:28.250
- Thank you so much for
talking to me, I love you.

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.991
- Oh! You're welcome!

00:05:29.991 --> 00:05:32.244
- Well, happy Mother's Day, momma.

00:05:32.244 --> 00:05:37.244
It's a really amazing thing
and I feel like I have

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:42.259
a deeper understanding of it
and a greater perspective.

00:05:42.832 --> 00:05:44.573
I love you very much.

00:05:44.573 --> 00:05:45.734
- I love you too!

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:47.243
- Thanks for being my mom.

00:05:54.522 --> 00:05:55.945
- OK, talk to you then, bye-bye!

00:05:55.945 --> 00:05:57.895
- Bye!

00:05:57.895 --> 00:05:59.032
- How do we get out of this now?

00:05:59.032 --> 00:06:00.974
(laughter)

00:06:00.974 --> 00:06:04.370
- [Keith's mom] Bye!
- Bye.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:05.543
That was classic.

